%N A296782 Detour index of the n-permutation star graph and the n-Bruhat graph.
%C A296782 For n >= 4, both graph families are strongly Hamiltonian-laceable, giving detour distances n!-1 between permutations of opposite parity and n!-2 between distinct permutations of the same parity; see Hsieh, Chen and Ho, and Araki and Kikuchi. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Jul 29 2018 [Updated by _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 28 2026]
%H A296782 Toru Araki and Yosuke Kikuchi, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ins.2007.01.017">Hamiltonian laceability of bubble-sort graphs with edge faults</a>, Information Sciences 177 (2007), 2679-2691.
%H A296782 Sun-Yuan Hsieh, Gen-Huey Chen, and Chin-Wen Ho, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1002/1097-0037(200012)36:4%3C225::AID-NET3%3E3.0.CO;2-G">Hamiltonian-laceability of star graphs</a>, Networks 36 (2000), 225-232.
%H A296782 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/BruhatGraph.html">Bruhat Graph</a>.
%H A296782 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/DetourIndex.html">Detour Index</a>.
%H A296782 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PermutationStarGraph.html">Permutation Star Graph</a>.
%F A296782 a(n) = n!*(2*(n!)^2 - 5*n! + 4)/4 for n >= 4, from strong Hamiltonian laceability (Hsieh, Chen and Ho). - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 28 2026
%t A296782 Join[{0, 1, 63}, Table[n! (2 (n!)^2 - 5 n! + 4)/4, {n, 4, 20}]] (* _Eric W. Weisstein_, Oct 28 2026 *)
